Subject: [PATCH] playerbots: a ground move the navmesh cannot carry is refused, not flown

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

PathGenerator, at the core pin, gives a player a two-point straight path
whenever the navmesh cannot carry the move in one piece:
- no polygon at either end. `bool path = creature ? creature->CanFly() : true`
  treats every player as able to fly, so the type is NORMAL | NOT_USING_PATH;
- a route longer than the point limit (74 points, about 296 yards).
  BuildShortcut() runs and the type is PATHFIND_SHORT;
- a tile that is not loaded (NORMAL | NOT_USING_PATH).
PointMovementGenerator and MoveSplineInit::MoveTo refuse only NOPATH, and
MoveSplineInit::MoveTo falls back to the same two-point line even then. So a
ground move to a point the navmesh will not carry runs as a ruler-straight
spline at run speed. It goes through the air where the ground dips and through
the rock where it rises.

MovementAction::MoveTo is the funnel every bot move goes through, and neither
of its branches refuses such a path. The exact_waypoint branch hands the point
straight to MovePoint. SearchForBestPath accepts a path type with a bit test,
(type & (NORMAL | INCOMPLETE)), so NORMAL | SHORT and NORMAL | NOT_USING_PATH
both pass. NewRpgBaseAction::MoveWorldObjectTo and the `go x;y;z` command call
it with no distance bound.

Measured on the dev realm (wow-overseer issue 2937): a family leader sent to a
trainer 3000 yards away ran a straight line to the trainer's spawn, 186 yards
above the ground at its highest. The position was read every 30 s, and each
step was the same vector at 7 yards a second. The next line, to the same spawn,
ran 33 to 49 yards under the hills. A follower ran beside it 0.3 yards away.

WHAT IT DOES

Before either branch of MoveTo launches a ground move (generatePath true),
RefusesGroundShortcut asks PathGenerator for the path the move would take. A
move longer than 20 yards whose path is a straight line rather than a route
(NOT_USING_PATH, SHORT, NOPATH or SHORTCUT) is refused: MoveTo returns false
and nothing is launched, so the caller's own fallback runs. For
NewRpgBaseAction::MoveFarTo that is the forward cone, whose steps are 70 yards
or less.

Unchanged:
- a move the navmesh carries;
- a move of 20 yards or less, such as stepping back onto the mesh;
- a flying or swimming bot (generatePath is false, and a straight line is how
  it moves);
- a bot on a transport, in a battleground (which has its own
  DisableMoveSplinePath switch) or with UNIT_STATE_IGNORE_PATHFINDING;
- the vehicle branch.

The cost is one PathGenerator call, made only for moves longer than 20 yards.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

An upstream MoveTo that checks the path type before it launches a move, or a
core whose PointMovementGenerator does not launch a straight line for a ground
player.

APPLIES TO

  repo: https://github.com/quadseven/mod-playerbots.git
  SHA:  40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130 (the pin), after patches
        0001 to 0052 of this directory (checked with git apply, then by
        grepping the two new call sites). Mirrors patch 0053 of the
        build's patch directory. It touches MovementActions.cpp (MoveTo) and
        MovementActions.h.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/MovementActions.cpp b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/MovementActions.cpp
index f9da49ac..580811b5 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/MovementActions.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/MovementActions.cpp
@@ -166,6 +166,50 @@ bool MovementAction::MoveToLOS(WorldObject* target, bool ranged)
     return false;
 }
 
+// A GROUND MOVE THE NAVMESH CANNOT CARRY IS REFUSED, NOT FLOWN (wow-overseer
+// issue 2937). PathGenerator hands a player a two-point straight path whenever
+// the navmesh cannot carry the move in one piece: no polygon at either end
+// (it treats every player as able to fly, so the type is NORMAL |
+// NOT_USING_PATH), a route longer than its point limit (BuildShortcut with
+// PATHFIND_SHORT) or a missing tile. PointMovementGenerator and
+// MoveSplineInit::MoveTo then launch that line, and launch it even on NOPATH.
+// The character runs a ruler-straight line at run speed through the air where
+// the ground dips and through the rock where it rises: measured, a leader 186
+// yards above the Burning Steppes on a 3000-yard line to the trainer it was
+// sent to, then 49 yards under the hills on the next one.
+//
+// Nothing below changes a move the navmesh can carry, a move of a stride or
+// less (stepping back onto the mesh), a flying or swimming bot (generatePath is
+// false there and a straight line is how it moves) or a battleground, whose
+// movement has its own DisableMoveSplinePath switch.
+static constexpr float GROUND_SHORTCUT_STRIDE_YARDS = 20.0f;
+
+static bool GroundMoveLeavesTheGround(uint32 pathType, float distance)
+{
+    if (distance <= GROUND_SHORTCUT_STRIDE_YARDS)
+        return false;
+    return (pathType & (PATHFIND_NOT_USING_PATH | PATHFIND_SHORT | PATHFIND_NOPATH | PATHFIND_SHORTCUT)) != 0;
+}
+
+bool MovementAction::RefusesGroundShortcut(float x, float y, float z, bool generatePath)
+{
+    if (!generatePath || bot->GetTransport() || bot->InBattleground() ||
+        bot->HasUnitState(UNIT_STATE_IGNORE_PATHFINDING))
+        return false;
+    float const distance = bot->GetExactDist(x, y, z);
+    if (distance <= GROUND_SHORTCUT_STRIDE_YARDS)
+        return false;
+    PathGenerator path(bot);
+    path.CalculatePath(x, y, z, false);
+    if (!GroundMoveLeavesTheGround(path.GetPathType(), distance))
+        return false;
+    LOG_DEBUG("playerbots",
+              "{} refuses a {:.0f}-yard ground move to ({:.1f}, {:.1f}, {:.1f}): path type {} is a straight line, not "
+              "a route (wow-overseer issue 2937)",
+              bot->GetName(), distance, x, y, z, static_cast<uint32>(path.GetPathType()));
+    return true;
+}
+
 bool MovementAction::MoveTo(uint32 mapId, float x, float y, float z, bool /*idle*/, bool /*react*/, bool normal_only,
                             bool exact_waypoint, MovementPriority priority, bool lessDelay, bool backwards)
 {
@@ -216,6 +260,9 @@ bool MovementAction::MoveTo(uint32 mapId, float x, float y, float z, bool /*idle
         float distance = bot->GetExactDist(x, y, z);
         if (distance > 0.01f)
         {
+            if (RefusesGroundShortcut(x, y, z, generatePath))
+                return false;
+
             if (bot->IsSitState())
                 bot->SetStandState(UNIT_STAND_STATE_STAND);
 
@@ -243,6 +290,9 @@ bool MovementAction::MoveTo(uint32 mapId, float x, float y, float z, bool /*idle
         float distance = bot->GetExactDist(x, y, modifiedZ);
         if (distance > 0.01f)
         {
+            if (RefusesGroundShortcut(x, y, modifiedZ, generatePath))
+                return false;
+
             if (bot->IsSitState())
                 bot->SetStandState(UNIT_STAND_STATE_STAND);
 
